# Tasks: checked spec

Tasks are codebase objects with history, as definitions are ([TASKS.md](../../docs/spec/TASKS.md)). This
document states what the task model promises: how a task is stored and read back, how its fields are
set from the command line, how an id is found and how lists are ordered (task 1ab6c044). Merging two
branches' tasks is stated in [Codebase.Spec](./Codebase.Spec.mdl) R-10. Written in the order of the
process (D92).

## Extensions

| Term | URI |
| --- | --- |
| `api` | `org.dxos.deus.api@1.0` |
| `req` | `org.dxos.deus.req@1.0` |

## APIs

```mdl
api A-1: the task model
  signatures:
  - Tasks.toSexp : Task -> Sexp
  - Tasks.fromSexp : Sexp -> Task
  - Tasks.setField : Task -> Text -> Text -> {Throw Text} Task
  - Tasks.link : Task -> Attachment -> Task
  - Tasks.find : Map Text Task -> Text -> {Throw Text} Task
  - Tasks.order : Task -> Task -> Int
  - Tasks.save : Text -> List Task -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Text
  - Tasks.current : Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Map Text Task
  - Tasks.resolveParent : Map Text Task -> Task -> {Throw Text} Task
```

## Requirements

```mdl
req R-1: a task's stored text reads back as the same task, whatever its title, labels, details and comments hold
  by: Tasks.Spec.storedTextReadsBack
```

```mdl
req R-2: a state is one of todo, doing, done, canceled, and a priority a name (none, urgent, high, medium, low) or 0..4; anything else is refused
  by: Tasks.Spec.statesAndPriorities
```

```mdl
req R-3: labels are set from a comma-separated list, trimmed, with empty items dropped
  by: Tasks.Spec.labelsFromAList
```

```mdl
req R-4: linking the same attachment twice keeps one link
  by: Tasks.Spec.linkIsIdempotent
```

```mdl
req R-5: a task is found by its id or by a prefix only it has; an unknown or ambiguous prefix is refused
  by: Tasks.Spec.findsByPrefix
```

```mdl
req R-6: lists show open tasks first, then by priority with none last, then by title
  by: Tasks.Spec.orderOpenPriorityTitle
```

```mdl
req R-7: a saved task is current on the branch, and saving it again unchanged writes no new change
  by: Tasks.Spec.savedTaskIsCurrent | Tasks.Spec.unchangedSaveWritesNothing
```

```mdl
req R-8: a parent is another task, named by its id or a prefix only it has and stored as its full id; a parent that is unknown, the task itself, or one of its descendants is refused
  by: Tasks.Spec.parentIsResolved | Tasks.Spec.parentRefusesCycles
```

## Laws

Each law is a test or theorem under `Tasks.Spec`; `deus ls Tasks.Spec.` lists them.
